```
Reason:
The code does not check if the memory allocation (`kmalloc`) fails. If it does, `rctx->ext` remains `NULL`, but `subreq->cryptlen` is still set to a potentially large value, leading to an out-of-bounds write when `pre_crypt()` accesses the uninitialized memory.

